From: IvyCZE <me@ivy.yt>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:57:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Embermine: 0005-wallpaper-colors-switch-and-accent

Add the "Use wallpaper colors" switch to Settings > Customize. It is on by default, hidden below Android 12, stored in fenix_preferences through Settings, and recreates the activity as soon as it changes.

When the switch is on and the theme is not private, EmbermineAccent copies only the accent slots from the Material You scheme into Firefox's ColorScheme: the primary family, secondaryContainer and inversePrimary. Tertiary follows the dynamic primary, so buttons, switches and links use the same hue. The selected tab outline and the accent and CFR gradients become two-tone gradients from the dynamic primary to the dynamic tertiary. Backgrounds, surfaces, neutrals and error colors stay Firefox's. Private mode and Android 11 and older keep the Firefox colors.

EmbermineAccentScheme is plain Kotlin and its JVM test covers the slot mapping and the gradient stops.

Co-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>

